  "notes": "{裂|さ}ける means to tear, split, or rip apart (happening on its own).\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: {自動詞|じどうし} (intransitive)\n- Pair: {裂|さ}く (transitive - to tear something)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {布|ぬの}が{裂|さ}ける: cloth tears\n- {傷口|きずぐち}が{裂|さ}ける: a wound splits open\n- {皮|かわ}が{裂|さ}ける: skin splits\n- {口|くち}が{裂|さ}けても: even if my mouth splits (= never, under any circumstances)\n\nASPECT (ている):\n{裂|さ}けている indicates the resulting state of being torn/split.\n\nHOMOPHONE DISTINCTION:\n- {裂|さ}ける: to tear, split\n- {避|さ}ける: to avoid\n- {割|さ}ける: to be able to spare/allocate",
